  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="25a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 25a</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="25a" corresp="#wit-g-a">Gif he þonne ne mage, gewylde man hine, swa hwæðer swa man mæge, swa cucne swa deadne, ⁊ niman eall þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he ahte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="25a" corresp="#wit-a">Gif he ne mage, þonne gewylde man hine, swa hwæðer man mage, swa cucne swa deadne, ⁊ niman eall þæt he age.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="25a" corresp="#wit-q">Si non possit, exuperetur, sicut alterutrum poterit, siue uiuus siue mortuus, et capiatur omne quod habebit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="25a" corresp="#wit-b">Gyf he ðonne ne mæge, gewylde man hine swa hwæðer swa man mæge, swa cwicne swa deadne, ⁊ nimen eall þæt he ah.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">If, however, he cannot [do so], they shall seize him as they can, either alive or dead, and they shall take all that he has.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Wenn er [dies] aber nicht kann, (dann A) bemächtige man sich seiner, wie man kann, entweder lebend oder todt; und sie sollen alles was er hat(te G) fortnehmen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But if he cannot [do this], (then, A) let him be overpowered however one can, alive or dead; and let them take everything he has (had, G).</ab>
        <note type="editorial">A and Ld's ‘age’ is better than G's ‘ahte’ (compare III Eg 7.1). Liebermann compares III Eg 7.1.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
